  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Controlled",
      "text": "Controlled `Slider`:\n\nControlled `RangeSlider`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "onChangeEnd",
      "text": "`onChangeEnd` callback is called when user the slider is stopped from being dragged or value is changed with keyboard.\nYou can use it as a debounced callback to avoid too frequent updates.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Control label",
      "text": "To change label behavior and appearance, set the following props:\n\n- `label` – formatter function, accepts value as an argument, set null to disable label, defaults to `f => f`\n- `labelAlwaysOn` – if true – label will always be displayed, by default label is visible only when user is dragging\n- `labelTransitionProps` – props passed down to the [Transition](/core/transition) component, can be used to customize label animation",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Decimal values",
      "text": "To use `Slider` with decimal values, set `min`, `max` and `step` props:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "minRange",
      "text": "Use `minRange` prop to control minimum range between `from` and `to` values\nin `RangeSlider`. The default value is `10`. The example below shows how to\nuse `minRange` prop to capture decimal values from the user:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Marks",
      "text": "Add any number of marks to slider by setting `marks` prop to an array of objects:\n\nNote that mark value is relative to slider value, not width:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Restrict selection to marks",
      "text": "Set `restrictToMarks` prop to restrict slider value to marks only. Note that in\nthis case `step` prop is ignored:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scale",
      "text": "You can use the `scale` prop to represent the value on a different scale.\n\nIn the following demo, the value `x` represents the value `2^x`. Increasing `x` by one increases the represented value by 2 to the power of `x`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inverted",
      "text": "You can invert the track with the `inverted` prop:\n\nExample of using [Styles API](/styles/styles-api/) to change `Slider` styles:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vertical slider",
      "text": "`Slider` and `RangeSlider` do not provide vertical orientation as it is very rarely used.\nIf you need this feature you can build it yourself with [use-move](/hooks/use-move/) hook.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Build custom slider",
      "text": "If `Slider` component does not meet your requirements, you can build a custom slider with [use-move](/hooks/use-move/) hook:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "`Slider` and `RangeSlider` components are accessible by default:\n\n- Thumbs are focusable\n- When the user uses mouse to interact with the slider, focus is moved to the slider track, when the user presses arrows focus is moved to the thumb\n- Value can be changed with arrows with step increment/decrement\n\nTo label component for screen readers, add labels to thumbs:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Keyboard interactions",
      "text": "  data={[\n\n      key: 'ArrowRight/ArrowUp',\n      description: 'Increases slider value by one step',\n    },\n\n      key: 'ArrowLeft/ArrowDown',\n      description: 'Decreases slider value by one step',\n    },\n\n  ]}\n/>",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
